        <p>War Subscriptions.</p>
        <p>COUNTY BOROUGH OF WARRINGTON. WAR REFUGEES. Mrs. Mocatta and the Misses Nunnerley hav- ing generously placed the house No. 21, Stanley- street, at the disposal of the Local Committee, the Committee are anxious to receive gifts or loans of beds, bedding, and other furniture for fitting up the house. The Committee will also be glad to receive con- tributions in money or food. Ladies and gentlemen willing to help may ascertain the best way of doing so by inquiring at St. Austin's on any day except Saturday and Sunday, between the hours of 11 and 12.30. Subscriptions to the "War Refugees Fund" should be sent to the Borough Treasurer at Bank House.</p>
        <p>PETER PEACOCK, Mayor. LIST OF SUBSCRIPTIONS. s. d. 114 4 0 Gross receipts from Belgian Tea, per 14 9 0 PAir orcse. e dSavage caonl dl e jo. sn. Royal Court Theatre, per Mrs. Robert Pemberton. slitaakyeAnaral.the • 5 0 0 George W. Brooke. 3 2 5 Warrington Ragged School, propor- tion of proceeds of Service of Song. ' 2 2 0 H. Reading and Elijah Lunt (each). 2 0 0 J. J. Owen. 1 1 0 A. J. T. Redhead, Dr. Howard, and each F. Beswick. 1 0 0 Mrs. Ransome (8 weeks con. at 2/6). 017 3 Collection at St. Clement's Mission. 010 0 Beamont School Top Class Girls, per each Misses Taylor and Clark, Mrs. Toul- min, and Miss A. Beswick, 0 7 3 Collected at Appleton Rifle Club. Total amount contributed to 23rd October: £531 17s. 9d. GIFTS.</p>
        <p>FURNITURE AND LINEN.—Mrs. Looker, Naylor-street; Mrs. H. Sileock, Mrs. Clive, and Mrs. Chambers. PROVISIONS.—Mrs. Healey, St. Barnabas? Y.M. Bible Class, per Mr. Dimelow ; Mrs. Lindley, Mme. De Witte, Mr. John Reid. Mr. Birtles, Mr. Bowman, Mr. Buck, Mr. Hall- wood, Mrs. Frost, Mrs. Rylands, Mr. W. Bate, Mr. T. Dutton, Mr. Owen, Mr. J. Lightfoot, Crowton ; Mr. J. Lightfoot, Earlestown ; Mr. Hepherd, Rixton; Mr. Alker, Bewssy-road; Mrs. Freeman, Master Curran, and Mr. Guest. CLOTHING.—Mrs. Bedell, Mr. Isherwood, Mrs. Gandy, Mrs. Rathbone, Mr. Roberts, Women's Sewing Class, Glazebury, per Mrs. Hartley; Mrs. Geary, Mrs. Voisey, Mrs. Sileock, Mrs. Fry, Mrs. H. Joseph, Mrs. Freeman, Mrs. Dell, Mr. J. Warburton, Mrs. Armitage, Miss Benn, Miss M. E. Taylor. Mrs. Richardson, Miss Harvey, Mrs. Owen Smith, Master R. Gornall, Mrs. T. Locker, Mr. Bowman, Mr. Vere Davies, Mr. Fairhurst. Dr. Langdale, Mrs. Gough. Dr. Bowden, the Mayor, Alderman Peacock; Mrs. Lee-Jones, Mrs. H. Sileock.</p>
        <p>CIOUNTY BOROUGH OF WARRINGTON. IL -1 TOBACCO FUND FOR THE 2ND SOUTH LANCASHIRES (THE WARRINGTON LINE BATTALION) SERVING AT THE FRONT. s. d. 2 2 0 Fred Ha</p>
