        <p>BONFIRES. to Sir,—One agrees with Mrs. Pemberton ase,t the destruction of hedges, &amp;c., by boys in c,l,l;re's of wood for bonfires; this, practice rerl:net prompt and strong measures. One ra'-off agree, however, that children when setting a few fireworks around a fire in their 3011- backyard are mimicking the fires on the no, tinent. Children's bonfires are purelY cent. There are as yet no restrictions w ever to such bonfires in this district,, oit quote the "Manchester Evening News,, oe. will be time enough to stop bonfires and works when the Government so orders!' T. PEINu'</p>
