        <p>HIPPODROME. 7.0. TWICE NIGHTLY. 9.0. ' MONDAY NEXT, OCT. 26th, and during the week. THE CORNER-GREY MUSICAL NOVELTY: SY M PHON I A . BROTHERS ERARD, Comedy Fiddlers. JAMES DIXON, Brilliant Baritone. JIMMIE PULLIN, Comedian. GEO. SHELDON and RAWSON BUCKLEY'S CO. in the one-act play: "CAPT. CARELESS, V.C." SIMS &amp; HURSTE, in "The Captain and the Mate." JOCK MILLS, SCOTCH COMEDIAN. Gallery, 2d.; Pit, 4d.; Grand Circle, 6d.; Stalls, is.</p>
        <p>STAR KINEMA 6.50 EVERY EVENING-9.0. MONDAY, TUESDAY and WEDNESDAY: " CHILD OF MY liEllff." THURSDAY, FRIDAY and SATURDAY: " TIIE JEW." Matinees: Monday, Thursday, Friday &amp; Saturday, at 3.0. Prices: la., 6d., 4d., 3d., and 2d. Tel. 634.</p>
        <p>. -- T CARTER, Accountant, Summerville GP • Gardens, Latchford Without. —Private Audits, Balance-sheets, etc. Students taken for Commer- cial Subjects. WOLFENDEN HARRISON, Humorist and Elocutionist, will give his services at Enter- tainments of any kind in aid of the Relief Funds tor our Soldiers.—Apply J. Harrison, 51, Ripley- street, Warrington.</p>
        <p>I'.—., AIRCOMBINGS made up 28. per oz. COVERLETTE TAILS OF } FrMl' HAIR FRAMES. PURE From Is. 6d. each. HAIR. 5/6 T. S. BROWN, 3, LEECE-STREET, (Car Station). LIVERPOOL.</p>
        <p>CROSFIELD'S RECREATION GROUND, HOOD-LANE, WARRINGTON. Certain Excavation is required at above ground. Full particulars and copy of Specifica- tion may be obtained from Mr. P. Smith, Messrs. Joseph Crosfield and Sons, Ltd., on or after Wednesday, 28th inst. Tenders to be' submitted on or before Wednesday. November 4th.</p>
        <p>COUNTY BOROUGH OF WARRINGTON. The Finance Committee of the Corpora- tion invite TENDERS from the local Printers and Stationers for the Supply of PRINTING and STATIONERY required by the various departments of the Corporation during the next twelve months. Specifications, with conditions as to rates of wages and hours of labour, can be obtained on and after Monday next, from the Borough Treasurer, Sankey-street, on deposit of los., which will be returnea on receipt of a bona- fide Tender. Tenders, securely fastened, addressed .to the Chairman of the Finance Committee, and endorsed "Tenders for Printing and Stationery," must be delivered to the Borough Treasurer, on or before Saturday, the ' 14th November, 1914. J. LYON WHITTLE. Town Clerk. Town Hall, Warrington, 23rd October, 1914.</p>
        <p>BEL G lAN REFUGEES' HOME, BEECHWOOD, LYMM. THIS HOME WILL BE OPEN TO VISITORS ON MONDAY NEXT, OCTOBER 20th, from 10 a.m. to 4 p.m. Admission: SIXPENCE.</p>
        <p>RED CROSS.—It has been arranged to hold a Rummage Sale in the Kendrick-street School Rooms on Saturday, Nov. 21st, 1914, in aid of local Red Cross work. Parcels will be called for on Nov. 20th, if donors will kindly communicate with the Hon. Sec. Mrs. W. H. Tickell, Roseneath, Marl- borough Crescent, Latchford. If this date in incon- venient, parcels may be sent direct to the Hon. Treasurer, Miss Bogstrom, 99, Bewsey-road, War- rington, who will be glad to receive them at any time.</p>
